Um, I asked the LLM a bunch of questions and it tells me this is more elegant

01:03:06.971 --> 01:03:08.290
or this is a better way to do things.

01:03:08.571 --> 01:03:09.811
I skipped past that.

01:03:10.050 --> 01:03:13.571
Anything that comes out of the LLM that is judgment based, even if the

01:03:13.571 --> 01:03:16.290
judgment is 100% correct, I don't want to read it.

01:03:16.331 --> 01:03:17.290
I don't want to hear it.

01:03:17.290 --> 01:03:19.290
You are not a human being with stake in the game.

01:03:19.491 --> 01:03:22.010
I simply do not care what you have to say.

01:03:22.410 --> 01:03:24.370
I, the accuracy doesn't matter.

01:03:24.410 --> 01:03:27.290
Even if it's a hundred percent correct, it doesn't matter.

01:03:27.290 --> 01:03:29.091
I do not want to hear what a robot has to say.

01:03:29.331 --> 01:03:32.091
And as a consequence, I think that from the documentation perspective, the

01:03:32.091 --> 01:03:36.971
very opinionated documentation, that's where I would say, keep the LLM away from

01:03:36.971 --> 01:03:37.091
it.

01:03:37.091 --> 01:03:40.691
I really do not want to read that very, very violently.

01:03:40.691 --> 01:03:41.491
Do not want to read that.

01:03:42.370 --> 01:03:42.650
Right.

01:03:42.691 --> 01:03:46.010
It's the, I don't want to ask people to read something that I

01:03:46.010 --> 01:03:47.451
couldn't be bothered to write.

01:03:47.650 --> 01:03:51.770
I think I'm still there, but I agree.

01:03:51.770 --> 01:03:57.130
I was saying just for things like, like doc strings, like, uh, no, that's more

01:03:57.130 --> 01:03:57.571
than fair.

